1. Microsoft Open Specifications material
-----------------------------------------

1.1 WBXML token tables

This project includes a limited transcription of WBXML token tables from
the following Microsoft Open Specifications document:

    [MS-ASWBXML]: Exchange ActiveSync: WAP Binary XML (WBXML) Algorithm
    Document version: v20250520 (release 2025-05-20)
    Relevant section: 2.1.2.1 (code page / tag token tables)
    Source:
    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/exchange_server_protocols/ms-aswbxml/
    Retrieved: 2026-11-04

The transcribed data (page number, tag name, token value) is stored in
  - src/davbridge/eas/tags_table.py (generated code tables), and
  - tests/data/eas_tags.txt (plain-text copy used to verify the code tables).
The tables are reproduced to the extent technically necessary to encode and
decode ActiveSync WBXML messages and to reject unsupported commands in a
defined way. They contain identifiers and numeric values only; no
descriptive text of the specification is reproduced.

1.2 Other Microsoft Open Specifications used as implementation references

The implementation was written from the public specifications listed in
docs/protocol-sources.md. Except for the token tables described above, no
text, schema or example of those documents is reproduced in this repository
beyond short identifiers (element names, command names, status codes, URL
paths) that are required for interoperability. Test fixtures are
synthetic.

Copyright in the Microsoft documentation remains with Microsoft
